# Every text file is LF in the repo and in every checkout, Windows included
# (2026-10-04). With core.autocrlf=true a Windows checkout used to be CRLF, and
# test/verify-quick-calc.cjs failed there on line endings alone, so a local run
# meant exporting with `git -c core.autocrlf=false archive` first.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Build output is committed and served byte-for-byte by both hosts
# (tools/build.mjs). Git must never rewrite its line endings: a Windows
# checkout with core.autocrlf=true would otherwise hand CI different bytes
# from the ones the ?v= content hashes and the vendor SRI check were taken on.
compiled/** -text linguist-generated=true
vendor/** -text
